Uncomputed analytics metrics no longer render as 0.0000 in the node table
================================================================================

Context
-------
User report: "Pagerank is to zero, like betweenness, closeness and clustering".

Investigation found two separate things, only one of which is a bug.

Not a bug: the admin toggle is currently off (verified via
`GET /settings/analytics-job-enabled` → `enabled=false, source=admin`, the state
it was deliberately reset to at the end of the previous session). With the
toggle off, a 7.6M-triple graph routes to engine-side aggregation, and
`PushdownMetrics.UNAVAILABLE_METRICS` is exactly
`("pagerank", "betweenness", "closeness", "clustering")` — the four metrics the
user saw as zero. Those four being absent is the documented contract for that
mode, not a regression.

The bug: `_renderPagerankTable` did not honour that contract. Uncomputed metrics
are stored as `0`, and every cell was formatted with `toFixed(4)`, so an
uncomputed metric printed `0.0000` — visually identical to a genuine measured
zero (a leaf node really does have betweenness 0). The chart-level notices did
explain the situation, but the node-detail table silently contradicted them by
presenting non-results as results. The table also sorted by PageRank
unconditionally, so in engine-side mode it ordered rows by a column that was all
zeros — an arbitrary order beneath a header implying a ranking.

Changes
-------
1. src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_analytics.html
   - `cell()` now checks `unavailable_metrics` first and returns an em dash with
     a "Not computed in this mode" tooltip, short-circuiting before `toFixed`.
     A genuine zero still prints `0.0000`, so the two cases are distinguishable.
   - `cell()` prefixes `≈` to metrics listed in `approximate_metrics`, so the
     sampled betweenness/closeness columns in job mode are not read as exact.
   - Ranking key is chosen at render time: PageRank when it was computed,
     otherwise degree (which pushdown does compute), so the order is meaningful
     in every mode.
   - New `_setPagerankTableNote()` renders a note above the table stating what
     the rows are ranked by, which columns were not computed, and which are
     sampled estimates. It hides itself when everything is exact, so the
     in-memory mode is visually unchanged.
   - New `#pagerankTableNote` element in the card body.

2. tests/units/front/test_analytics_unavailable_metrics.py (new)
   - Asserts the dash branch precedes and returns before `toFixed`, that the
     comparator uses `rankBy` rather than a hard-coded `.pagerank`, that the note
     covers all three conditions and hides itself when unnecessary, and that the
     pre-existing chart notices still distinguish "not computed" from
     "all values are 0".

Verification
------------
- The panel's inline JS parses (`node --check` on the extracted script block).
- The `cell()` + `rankBy` logic was mirrored in a scratch harness and run for
  all three modes. in_memory: ranks by pagerank, real zeros still `0.0000`.
  pushdown: ranks by degree, four columns dashed, degree numeric. job: ranks by
  pagerank, betweenness/closeness prefixed `≈`.

