Deploy the graph-analytics job to Databricks (three blocking bugs fixed)
================================================================================

Context
-------
User asked for the serverless graph-analytics job to be uploaded so they could
run it. The job had never been deployed. Getting there required fixing three
bugs, each of which blocked the deploy at a later stage than the last.

Outcome: the job is deployed and runnable —
`[dev benoit_cayla] ontobricks-07x-graph-analytics`, job_id 822506438871868.
The apps did NOT deploy (see "Still blocked").

Changes
-------
1. resources/graph_analytics.job.yml — invalid YAML.
   The earlier `--pivots` / `--pagerank-iterations` additions were mis-indented:
   four list items nested under `exclude_predicates` instead of being siblings,
   and the `pagerank_iterations` / `pivots` job parameters dedented out of the
   `parameters:` list. The file did not parse.

   Blast radius was much wider than the job: the Databricks CLI loads every
   file under `resources/` for any bundle-aware command, so even
   `databricks auth describe` failed with `yaml: line 52: did not find expected
   '-' indicator`. This is why the previous session concluded that
   `bundle validate` was blocked by an expired OAuth token — the token was also
   expired, but the YAML error was the first failure and masked it.

2. scripts/_internal/_deploy-preflight.sh — sibling source resolved from the
   caller's SCRIPT_DIR.
   The file sourced `${SCRIPT_DIR:-<own dir>}/_lakebase-diag.sh`. It is *sourced*
   by scripts/deploy.sh, where SCRIPT_DIR is already `scripts/`, so the `:-`
   default never applied and the lookup missed `scripts/_internal/`. Now resolved
   from `BASH_SOURCE` into a private `_PREFLIGHT_DIR`, leaving the caller's
   SCRIPT_DIR untouched (deploy.sh still needs it). Fallout from 2c6ef76.

3. scripts/_internal/_render-app-yaml.py — REPO_ROOT off by one.
   `Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent` resolved to `scripts/` after the file
   moved into `_internal/`, so it looked for `scripts/app.yaml.template`. Now
   `parents[2]`. Same 2c6ef76 fallout; no sibling script shares the pattern.

4. tests/units/settings/test_bundle_job_resource.py (new) — 12 tests.
   None of the above was reachable from the suite, because nothing parses the
   bundle or exercises the deploy scripts. Now covered:
   - every file under `resources/` and `databricks.yml` is valid YAML;
   - each `{{job.parameters.X}}` is declared and each declared parameter is
     used; task parameters strictly alternate flag/value (a mis-indent drops a
     value and shifts every later pair);
   - the serverless `environment_key` has a matching `environments` entry;
   - `python_file` exists in the repo and is not caught by a `sync.exclude`;
   - the job's own argparse accepts exactly the flags the bundle passes, so a
     flag drift fails here instead of at runtime in Spark;
   - both deploy-script path fixes, asserted behaviourally (the templates and
     the sourced sibling are resolved and confirmed to exist) rather than only
     by string match.

Verification
------------
- `make bundle-validate` → valid (4 pre-existing warnings for `sync.exclude`
  patterns that match no files: htmlcov, mlruns, mlartifacts, sphinx doctrees).
- Deployed via `make deploy-no-run`, chosen deliberately over `make deploy` so
  the running app is not restarted (see the uv.lock note below).
- Deployed job definition read back from the API: correct serverless
  `environments` (client "3"), all five flags wired, job parameter defaults
  `pagerank_iterations=20` / `pivots=64`.
- Uploaded source verified byte-identical to local (sha256 `ec94e93fd118191e`,
  34817 bytes) and confirmed to contain `_run_pivot_centrality` and the `md5(`
  pivot sampling, i.e. it is the current betweenness/closeness implementation.
- Full suite: uv run pytest -q -m "not scenario" → 3699 passed, 275 skipped,
