## Per-instance DAB target from DEFAULT_INSTANCE_ID

Context: Changing only DEFAULT_APP_NAME kept the same DAB target (and tfstate),
so Terraform treated it as a rename and destroyed the running app. Multi-instance
deploys need a distinct target per instance. DEFAULT_INSTANCE_ID is now the
single knob: it derives the app name and a suffixed DAB target
(``dev-lakebase-<id>``), and deploy.sh materialises that target before validate.

Changes:

1. scripts/deploy.config.sh
   Add DEFAULT_INSTANCE_ID / DEFAULT_DAB_BACKEND; derive DEFAULT_APP_NAME,
   DEFAULT_MCP_APP_NAME, and DEFAULT_DAB_TARGET from them. Resource keys stay
   static. Env-overridable for CI (DEFAULT_INSTANCE_ID=080 make deploy).
2. scripts/_internal/_ensure-instance-target.sh
   New helper writing resources/_generated_instance_target.yml for
   ``dev-lakebase-<id>`` / ``dev-<id>``; clears it for legacy ``dev`` /
   ``dev-lakebase``.
3. scripts/deploy.sh
   Source the helper and call ensure_instance_target before bundle validate;
   print Instance in the deploy banner; document instance targets.
4. databricks.yml
   Document that per-instance targets are generated and included via
   resources/*.yml; keep static ``dev`` / ``dev-lakebase`` for legacy.
5. scripts/_internal/_deploy-preflight.sh
   Rename-guard guidance now points at DEFAULT_INSTANCE_ID / separate targets.
6. .gitignore
   Ignore resources/_generated_instance_target.yml.
7. tests/units/settings/test_deploy_instance_id.py
   New coverage for derivation, target generation, and deploy wiring.
8. tests/units/settings/test_deploy_app_rename_guard.py
   Expect DEFAULT_INSTANCE_ID in the keep-old-app message.

