================================================================================
Fix: successful graph-analytics run reported as failed (SystemExit at exit)
================================================================================

Context:

Run 314895410340960 of ``[dev benoit_cayla] ontobricks-07x-graph-analytics``
(job 334933950622420) terminated with ``RUN_EXECUTION_ERROR`` even though the
analysis had completed: the driver log ends with
``wrote benoit_cayla.ontobricks.graph_metrics_bigcustomers_1 (1349202 nodes)``
followed by the ``ONTOBRICKS_GRAPH_ANALYTICS_SUMMARY`` line. The reported
error was ``SystemExit: 0``.

Root cause: Databricks serverless executes a ``spark_python_task`` file inside
an IPython shell (visible in the run output as the
``To exit: use 'exit', 'quit', or Ctrl-D`` warning from
``IPython/core/interactiveshell.py``). The module guard ended the process with
``raise SystemExit(main())``; that shell reports *any* raised ``SystemExit`` —
code 0 included — as an uncaught exception, so a clean run was recorded as a
failed workload and the app surfaced the analysis as failed.

Changes:

1. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py
   Replace ``raise SystemExit(main())`` with ``run_cli()``, which raises
   ``SystemExit`` only for a non-zero return so genuine failures still fail the
   run while a successful analysis exits normally.
2. tests/units/core/test_graph_analytics_job_exit.py (new)
   Five unit tests over ``run_cli``: return 0 and return ``None`` must not
   raise, a non-zero return must raise ``SystemExit`` with that code, argv is
   forwarded, and the module guard no longer calls ``raise SystemExit(main())``.

Follow-up noted, not changed:

- Two jobs now answer to the name ``[dev benoit_cayla] ontobricks-07x-graph-analytics``:
  334933950622420 (target ``dev-lakebase-07x``, current) and 822506438871868
  (target ``dev-lakebase``, orphaned by today's per-instance target split).
  ``LakeflowRunner.resolve_job_id`` warns and takes the first match, so the app
  can pick the stale one. Deleting the orphan is pending user confirmation.

